  "term": "Ammon’s horn",
  "definition": "Ammon’s horn is another name for the hippocampus, a curved ridge of gray matter that runs along the floor of the temporal horn of the lateral ventricle. The hippocampal formation includes the hippocampus proper, subiculum, and dentate gyrus, and some authors also include the entorhinal cortex.",
